WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
John, Chapter Eighteen.

2
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:10.533
When Jesus had spoken these words, he went forth with his disciples over the brook Cedron, where was a garden, into the which he entered, and his disciples.

3
00:00:10.533 --> 00:00:17.333
And Judas also, which betrayed him, knew the place: for Jesus ofttimes resorted thither with his disciples.

4
00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:25.733
Judas then, having received a band of men and officers from the chief priests and Pharisees, cometh thither with lanterns and torches and weapons.

5
00:00:25.733 --> 00:00:33.467
Jesus therefore, knowing all things that should come upon him, went forth, and said unto them, Whom seek ye?

6
00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:36.400
They answered him, Jesus of Nazareth.

7
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.600
Jesus saith unto them, I am he.

8
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.800
And Judas also, which betrayed him, stood with them.

9
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:48.400
As soon then as he had said unto them, I am he, they went backward, and fell to the ground.

10
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.467
Then asked he them again, Whom seek ye?

11
00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:53.467
And they said, Jesus of Nazareth.

12
00:00:53.467 --> 00:01:05.467
Jesus answered, I have told you that I am he: if therefore ye seek me, let these go their way: That the saying might be fulfilled, which he spake, Of them which thou gavest me have I lost none.

13
00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:10.933
Then Simon Peter having a sword drew it, and smote the high priest's servant, and cut off his right ear.

14
00:01:10.933 --> 00:01:13.467
The servant's name was Malchus.

15
00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:20.800
Then said Jesus unto Peter, Put up thy sword into the sheath: the cup which my Father hath given me, shall I not drink it?

16
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:33.333
Then the band and the captain and officers of the Jews took Jesus, and bound him, And led him away to Annas first; for he was father in law to Caiaphas, which was the high priest that same year.

17
00:01:33.333 --> 00:01:40.267
Now Caiaphas was he, which gave counsel to the Jews, that it was expedient that one man should die for the people.

18
00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:50.400
And Simon Peter followed Jesus, and so did another disciple: that disciple was known unto the high priest, and went in with Jesus into the palace of the high priest.

19
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.533
But Peter stood at the door without.

20
00:01:52.533 --> 00:02:00.133
Then went out that other disciple, which was known unto the high priest, and spake unto her that kept the door, and brought in Peter.

21
00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:06.267
Then saith the damsel that kept the door unto Peter, Art not thou also one of this man's disciples?

22
00:02:06.267 --> 00:02:07.867
He saith, I am not.

23
00:02:07.867 --> 00:02:17.867
And the servants and officers stood there, who had made a fire of coals; for it was cold: and they warmed themselves: and Peter stood with them, and warmed himself.

24
00:02:17.867 --> 00:02:21.733
The high priest then asked Jesus of his disciples, and of his doctrine.

25
00:02:21.733 --> 00:02:32.400
Jesus answered him, I spake openly to the world; I ever taught in the synagogue, and in the temple, whither the Jews always resort; and in secret have I said nothing.

26
00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.400
Why askest thou me?

27
00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:40.000
ask them which heard me, what I have said unto them: behold, they know what I said.

28
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:48.667
And when he had thus spoken, one of the officers which stood by struck Jesus with the palm of his hand, saying, Answerest thou the high priest so?

29
00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:54.667
Jesus answered him, If I have spoken evil, bear witness of the evil: but if well, why smitest thou me?

30
00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:58.533
Now Annas had sent him bound unto Caiaphas the high priest.

31
00:02:58.533 --> 00:03:00.800
And Simon Peter stood and warmed himself.

32
00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:05.600
They said therefore unto him, Art not thou also one of his disciples?

33
00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:08.400
He denied it, and said, I am not.

34
00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:16.800
One of the servants of the high priest, being his kinsman whose ear Peter cut off, saith, Did not I see thee in the garden with him?

35
00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:21.200
Peter then denied again: and immediately the cock crew.

36
00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:32.667
Then led they Jesus from Caiaphas unto the hall of judgment: and it was early; and they themselves went not into the judgment hall, lest they should be defiled; but that they might eat the passover.

37
00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:37.867
Pilate then went out unto them, and said, What accusation bring ye against this man?

38
00:03:37.867 --> 00:03:44.667
They answered and said unto him, If he were not a malefactor, we would not have delivered him up unto thee.

39
00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:49.600
Then said Pilate unto them, Take ye him, and judge him according to your law.

40
00:03:49.600 --> 00:04:00.133
The Jews therefore said unto him, It is not lawful for us to put any man to death: That the saying of Jesus might be fulfilled, which he spake, signifying what death he should die.

41
00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:07.333
Then Pilate entered into the judgment hall again, and called Jesus, and said unto him, Art thou the King of the Jews?

42
00:04:07.333 --> 00:04:12.933
Jesus answered him, Sayest thou this thing of thyself, or did others tell it thee of me?

43
00:04:12.933 --> 00:04:16.000
Pilate answered, Am I a Jew?

44
00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:21.200
Thine own nation and the chief priests have delivered thee unto me: what hast thou done?

45
00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:34.267
Jesus answered, My kingdom is not of this world: if my kingdom were of this world, then would my servants fight, that I should not be delivered to the Jews: but now is my kingdom not from hence.

46
00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:37.733
Pilate therefore said unto him, Art thou a king then?

47
00:04:37.733 --> 00:04:40.933
Jesus answered, Thou sayest that I am a king.

48
00:04:40.933 --> 00:04:47.600
To this end was I born, and for this cause came I into the world, that I should bear witness unto the truth.

49
00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.533
Every one that is of the truth heareth my voice.

50
00:04:50.533 --> 00:04:53.333
Pilate saith unto him, What is truth?

51
00:04:53.333 --> 00:04:59.733
And when he had said this, he went out again unto the Jews, and saith unto them, I find in him no fault at all.

52
00:04:59.733 --> 00:05:08.533
But ye have a custom, that I should release unto you one at the passover: will ye therefore that I release unto you the King of the Jews?

53
00:05:08.533 --> 00:05:12.933
Then cried they all again, saying, Not this man, but Barabbas.

54
00:05:12.933 --> 00:05:14.533
Now Barabbas was a robber.

